WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.401
There's so much that we don't know.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.435
And I know that we have been saying

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.004
a version of that for many, many weeks.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.071
But I would just like

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.173
to remind people that

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.175
the word that people,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.976
you know, supporting

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:10.677
Trump were putting out

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.945
yesterday was fanning

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.480
the flames of reports that the grand jury

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.748
was out for a month.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.716
So I think there's a lot of twists

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.717
to take on this.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.652
He is now going to go through the process

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.720
of getting arrested.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.856
And I think that that is going to be

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.524
much more jarring for him

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.492
than I think people realize.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.893
I've been told that he's been briefed

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.061
on what that will look like.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.462
It will involve fingerprinting

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.597
It's going to be unlike,

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.799
you know, a normal arraignment

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.634
because he's going to have Secret Service

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.569
and this is going to look different.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.038
This is somebody who has spent

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.506
more than four decades

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.374
trying to avoid being arrested

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.075
or being indicted.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.778
And so this is a really scary moment

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.446
for him, despite whatever he says.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.414
Now, you talk

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.314
to different people tonight.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.315
You hear he's fine.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.550
You talk to others who say that he's

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.751
very angry.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:52.919
I expect that we will be hearing

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.120
all of those emotions

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.255
going in various ways

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.090
for the coming days.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.892
I don't know what the fallout

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.193
is going to be politically.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.262
And I think this is the first time

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.764
that I can think of where he can't

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.299
he can't control this.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.301
He was able to control impeachment

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.403
in some way because Mitch McConnell

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.971
was on his side in the Senate trial,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:12.372
because House

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.807
Republicans were on his side.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:14.874
He was even able to control

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.342
the second impeachment to some extent

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.445
with the Mueller report

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.345
and the investigation.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.580
He was never going to get indicted

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.748
as a sitting president.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.483
And I think that he has an overconfidence

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.217
in his ability

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.253
to impact events by intimidation

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.056
tactics, by pushing out headlines.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.157
This is now

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.126
in the hands of whatever judge he draws

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.727
and what the voters think.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:34.894
There's

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.696
so many potential ripple effects

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.866
on public perception voter perception,

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.168
it's it's impossible

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.636
to kind of game it out

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:44.971
many steps in advance.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.541
It is in part because he's such a

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.243
an agent of uncertainty. Right.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.010
I mean, if you think about the fact

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.879
that we had a week of a news cycle

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.180
that he created by saying

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.582
he was going to get arrested on Tuesday,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.149
which literally

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.650
no one was saying in the news media,

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.551
and he created that.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:01:58.985
And then when that

00:01:58.985 --> 00:01:59.953
you also fundraised office

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:00.787
and he fundraised off it.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.288
And then when that day came and went,

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.723
he said, look, you know, it's

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.725
all falling apart. It didn't happen.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:06.626
So I don't know how

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.660
he's going to handle this.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.795
I do notice that,

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.129
you know,

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.396
he did not reiterate his call

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.097
for protests.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.699
I thought that was pretty striking.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.234
I did notice that Elise Stefanik,

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.768
a very close ally of his,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.603
put out a statement

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.771
saying that people should organize

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.639
peacefully.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.307
And everyone is trying to stress

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.041
that around him

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.743
because there are still these echoes

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.411
of January six. 20, 21.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:25.645
Yeah.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.913
And I think it's also something

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:27.547
we should note.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.448
We were talking about earlier

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.616
that we've both heard from people

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.551
is that they genuinely had an idea

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.052
that this may be falling apart,

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.021
that it may not actually be happening.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.456
This is from Trump's attorneys.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.191
There are a lot of attorneys around him

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:38.791
at the moment.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.192
He's hearing

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.426
from a lot of different voices,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.494
but that is why they were

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.562
so caught off guard

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.531
by how quickly this transpired today.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.031
Yeah, they had

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:45.598
they believe

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.833
the grand jury was not coming back.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.134
They believe that this was not going

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.103
to happen for a month.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.237
And then others of them,

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.071
not all of them,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.673
but others of them did believe

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.542
that the case was falling apart,

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:58.178
primarily on the word of Bob Costello,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.381
a Giuliani lawyer, and briefly,

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:02.515
Michael Cohen,

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.850
either lawyer or legal adviser,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.051
depending on who you believe,

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.586
who came in as a defense witness

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.687
in the grand jury in New York,

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.922
that you have the right to do that.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.124
There was no

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:11.791
evidence that

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.592
they ever offered

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.660
as to why they believe

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.527
that, just things

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.862
that people were hearing.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.397
And as I said,

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.132
Trump likes to create headlines

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.334
that he thinks influence events

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.635
that obviously did not happen here.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.770
And if anything, frankly,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.871
all the stories yesterday

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.538
about how the grand jury

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.472
was going to be off for a month

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.807
probably alleviate

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.642
a pressure valve for Bragg.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.310
It sort of

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.579
it took the heat down a little bit.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.613
I want to bring in David Urban

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.981
and in Van Jones.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:35.748
David,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.250
I mean, this is a remarkable

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:37.884
historic night

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:38.718
and wondering what your

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:42.088
your thoughts are on what happens now

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:42.956
Yeah.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:43.856
So, you know, Anderson,

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.358
I was just thinking back

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.125
20 years ago

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:46.793
when I was a

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.428
chief of staff of the state Senate,

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.762
and you had the impeachment

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.131
of Bill Clinton and Bill Clinton

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.499
you know, was impeached

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.667
and was acquitted similar

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.702
to President Trump

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.937
and then remained in office.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:58.304
And there,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:58.538
you know,

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.505
Ken Starr went away

00:03:59.505 --> 00:03:59.973
and special

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:00.807
prosecutor Robert

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.809
Ray was still lingered around.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.078
And there was the threat of

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.446
of Clinton being indicted

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.580
when he left office.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.482
That was always kind of out there.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.783
And the day

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.553
before he left in January, 19th, 2001,

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.922
a former special prosecutor,

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.091
Robert Ray, cut a deal with President

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.726
then President Clinton to

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.327
to not prosecute him. Right.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.630
And to let him surrender his law license

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.697
for five years,

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.599
pay a fine and put it aside.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:27.500
And, you know,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.602
there was a great deal of pressure on Ray

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.838
to indict him at the time and

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.538
and he didn't.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.840
And he said,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.073
you know,

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:34.574
the American

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.542
people and history will judge me

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.377
and judge

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.578
whether I did the right thing or not.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.113
And in retrospect,

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:40.580
you know,

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.582
I think Robert Ray did the right thing,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:43.883
and I'm not so sure.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.219
History will be so kind in this case

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.954
to Alvin Bragg.

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:48.921
Van Jones, what do you think

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.859
Well, I think that,

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:53.660
you know, Democrats,

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.161
progressives are swinging back

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:55.528
and forth

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.330
between being very, very worried

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.931
and very, very relieved.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.667
You know, on the one hand,

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.501
geez, you know,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.504
this case is hanging on a novel theory.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.172
It's not the insurrection.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.173
It's not the coup.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.341
It's not the election interference.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.643
It's a hush money payment.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.711
There's worry that this is

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:12.779
maybe not the bridge

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.881
to try to die on at the same time.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.016
I think a lot of people are saying

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:20.353
finally, finally, something

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.754
has happened

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.257
to get some kind of accountability here.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.725
You've had our social norms

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:26.893
run into the ground.

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:28.494
You've had our political norms

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.829
run to the ground,

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.230
at least our legal norms

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.532
are not being run into the ground.

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:33.299
In this case,

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.634
you have a prosecutor

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.802
who went to everyday,

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.470
ordinary Americans and said, here's

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.404
what I've got.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:39.472
Do you think it's chargeable?

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.673
And they said, yes,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.009
And I think that there is a sense

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:44.844
among some people

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.446
that somebody had to do

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:48.181
something at some point

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.082
and that everybody's

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.183
just kind of standing on the edge

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:50.850
of the swimming pool,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.451
looking at all

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.553
these prosecutors, all these these cases.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.988
And nothing has happened to happen yet.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:57.390
And so on the one hand,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.558
I think people are concerned

00:05:58.558 --> 00:05:59.125
and they're worried

00:05:59.125 --> 00:05:59.792
and they hope that this

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:00.727
and set some precedent

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:01.828
where presidents start

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:02.595
is getting prosecuted.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:03.863
There's real concern.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.264
But there is a sense

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.800
that finally some kind of accountability

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.936
may land on the doorstep of Donald Trump.

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:10.670
John Miller, it's

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.904
going to be interesting when,

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.239
you know, we're able to look back

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:13.706
and know

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:14.807
exactly what happened

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.175
in that grand jury room

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.577
over the last several weeks,

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:20.613
because clearly the the last witness

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.248
that was supportive

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:23.316
of the former president

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.418
or at least critical of Michael Cohen

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:28.588
made it seem to affect the course of

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.423
of the grand jury in some way.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.624
I mean, when you talk to people

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.126
in the district attorney's office

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.160
who have been following

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.130
the plan of the grand jury presentation,

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:41.033
they expected to get that indictment

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.535
back on Monday,

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:45.104
I think the 13th of March, two days ago.

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:45.505
Right.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:49.942
Putting Bob Costello in as a witness

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.377
in place of Donald Trump,

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.312
who they invited to testify

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:56.015
on his own behalf and declined

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:57.650
seem to be something

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.718
that they planned to do.

00:06:58.718 --> 00:06:59.652
And then put it

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.887
to the vote of the grand jury.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:01.954
I think

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:02.688
we don't know

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:03.723
what effect Costello's

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.325
testimony had on the grand jurors.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:08.161
That that is something

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.362
that's only in their minds.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.263
But we know the effect

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:11.431
it had on the prosecutors,

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.498
which is they

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.700
thought he did damage to their case

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.301
and they didn't

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.569
want him to be the last thing

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:17.970
grand jurors heard

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.539
before they went to a vote.

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:21.641
And the people I've been talking to said,

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:21.941
you know,

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:24.877
they went in two days of strategy to say,

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.946
what do we need to put in front of this

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.481
grand jury to repair that?

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:31.150
And so doubt into what Costello said.

